>
> That's a thing I've never understood so far... what's the real 
> difference between magic cancellation and magic resistance?

Magic resistance grants complete immunity to a certain set of
attacks.  Magic missiles and such bounce off.  Most of the attacks
protected against are available as rays, but some of them have
touch versions (wand/touch of death).

Magic cancellation grants statistical/partial immunity to a
*different* set of attacks.  Almost all bite attacks are blocked
to some extent by magic cancellation.

To two may sound similar, but they are different.

Magic resistance comes from GDSM, [oMR, Magicbane, and some Quest
artifacts.  It is often considered needed to ascend at least the
first few times.  Certainly you're in severe danger without it.
If you can conveniently arrange to have it redundantly, go for
it.

Magic cancellation comes in levels 0,1,2,3.  Each level is several
times as good as the one below it.  MC=3 cancels well over 90% of
the attacks it protects again.  MC comes from some body armor and
also from most cloaks.  Learn which cloaks offer MC=3 and wear one
of those.  If you select an MC=2 or worse cloak for other reasons
(displacement for example), make certain you where an MC=3 body
armor.

The usual ascension kit has MC=3, MR, reflection and an assortment
of intrinsic resistances (preferably all of them), plus good AC
and so on.

